# Line endings, declared rather than left to each machine's git config.
#
# Without this, git compared raw bytes: the repository stores LF, the working
# tree had drifted to CRLF, and so 24 files it had never touched showed as
# modified forever. That noise hides real changes and makes it easy to commit
# whole-file line-ending churn by accident.
#
# text=auto lets git detect text files and store them normalised as LF, which
# is what this repository already contains. eol=crlf checks them out with CRLF,
# which is what Visual Studio and the rest of the Windows toolchain expect - so
# the working tree keeps the endings it has now and git stops seeing a
# difference that was never a change.
* text=auto eol=crlf

# Binaries must never be touched: normalising an icon or an installer asset
# would corrupt it.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.snk binary
